// A direct call whose callee is not among the program's functions is replaced
// with `__patchestry_error("missing_call_...")`.  The placeholder is a valid
// statement, so the dropped-operation check cannot see that the call is gone.
// The default lift reports the substitution as a warning and still lowers;
// `-strict` turns the report into an error and stops before lowering.
//
// RUN: bash %strip-json-comments %s > %t.json
// RUN: %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -print-tu -output %t > %t.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=WARN %s --input-file %t.log
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=TU %s --input-file %t.c
// RUN: not %patchir-decomp -input %t.json -emit-cir -strict -output %t.strict > %t.strict.log 2>&1
// RUN: %file-check -vv -check-prefix=ERR %s --input-file %t.strict.log
// RUN: test ! -e %t.strict.cir
//
// WARN: Diag Warning: {{.*}}lossy lift [error-placeholder]: an operation in function 'strict_error_placeholder' could not be lifted and is replaced with __patchestry_error("missing_call_EXTERNAL_0000dead")
// WARN-NOT: Diag Error
// TU: __patchestry_error("missing_call_EXTERNAL_0000dead");
// ERR: Diag Error: {{.*}}lossy lift [error-placeholder]: an operation in function 'strict_error_placeholder' could not be lifted and is replaced with __patchestry_error("missing_call_EXTERNAL_0000dead")
// ERR: Skipping code generation due to prior diagnostics errors
